Q: How to embed phaser3 game into html A: <p>I suggest this answer.
You can specify an importmap in your HTML file:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script type=&quot;importmap&quot;&gt;
{
  &quot;imports&quot;: {
    &quot;phaser3&quot;: &quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/phaser@3.60.0/dist/phaser.esm.js&quot;
  }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>This way, in your javascript file,
you will be able to import from &quot;phaser3&quot;
(or whatever moniker your importmap specifies
for the library you want to import).</p>
<p>If you use it locally, your script
should be written like this (the 'module' part).</p>
<pre><code>&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot;&gt;
 import * as Phaser from &quot;phaser3&quot;;
..
</code></pre>
<p>Otherwise, when you include your js script, be sure to give it type 'module'.</p>
